[[:db/retract 17592186134311 :question/answer-fields 17592186131905] {:db/id 17592186133793 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7bb7823-c38b-5250-a2f7-3b306162dae1" "question-44c51145-6075-534b-b54c-46371542f3eb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7bb7823-c38b-5250-a2f7-3b306162dae1" :question/id #uuid "c7bb7823-c38b-5250-a2f7-3b306162dae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40736" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]},\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{17}{6} \\\\ \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{17}{6} \\\\ \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=\\frac{17}{6},$ $b=\\frac{11}{6},$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{(\\frac{17}{6})}{(\\frac{11}{6})}=\\frac{17}{11}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-219cb7dd-0360-5f51-af53-0c31b7c77c47"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-219cb7dd-0360-5f51-af53-0c31b7c77c47" :answer-field/id #uuid "219cb7dd-0360-5f51-af53-0c31b7c77c47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1326ecd9-681d-55f9-841c-c7013851f621" :answer-field/choices ["answer-292aa1fd-4f1b-5b3f-b502-e340aa086aa9" "answer-05da9795-05f5-5040-9da5-00cee056fe08" "answer-502fbad5-6108-585e-9a6e-c3c7e917352d" "answer-1326ecd9-681d-55f9-841c-c7013851f621" "answer-048ef5c8-0a10-53a5-bbcf-1d721a524144"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-292aa1fd-4f1b-5b3f-b502-e340aa086aa9" :answer/id #uuid "292aa1fd-4f1b-5b3f-b502-e340aa086aa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05da9795-05f5-5040-9da5-00cee056fe08" :answer/id #uuid "05da9795-05f5-5040-9da5-00cee056fe08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-502fbad5-6108-585e-9a6e-c3c7e917352d" :answer/id #uuid "502fbad5-6108-585e-9a6e-c3c7e917352d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1326ecd9-681d-55f9-841c-c7013851f621" :answer/id #uuid "1326ecd9-681d-55f9-841c-c7013851f621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-048ef5c8-0a10-53a5-bbcf-1d721a524144" :answer/id #uuid "048ef5c8-0a10-53a5-bbcf-1d721a524144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-44c51145-6075-534b-b54c-46371542f3eb" :question/id #uuid "44c51145-6075-534b-b54c-46371542f3eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-40737" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]},\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=-\\frac{1}{2},$ $b=2,$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}=-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5ce877fc-f404-5538-a461-7601462b178c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ce877fc-f404-5538-a461-7601462b178c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce877fc-f404-5538-a461-7601462b178c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c1253b4-be89-5b75-90d7-9bf16f52d17f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c1253b4-be89-5b75-90d7-9bf16f52d17f" "answer-194427ad-263d-5d8c-83c2-9e6a530a1d0d" "answer-18fa685c-26d9-50c3-9545-5630e0f95fcd" "answer-a926e36b-6239-5512-942a-761db7b00ee5" "answer-f308a53e-6685-5d66-b2f6-d1b95a0af889"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c1253b4-be89-5b75-90d7-9bf16f52d17f" :answer/id #uuid "5c1253b4-be89-5b75-90d7-9bf16f52d17f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-194427ad-263d-5d8c-83c2-9e6a530a1d0d" :answer/id #uuid "194427ad-263d-5d8c-83c2-9e6a530a1d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18fa685c-26d9-50c3-9545-5630e0f95fcd" :answer/id #uuid "18fa685c-26d9-50c3-9545-5630e0f95fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a926e36b-6239-5512-942a-761db7b00ee5" :answer/id #uuid "a926e36b-6239-5512-942a-761db7b00ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f308a53e-6685-5d66-b2f6-d1b95a0af889" :answer/id #uuid "f308a53e-6685-5d66-b2f6-d1b95a0af889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133795 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0934e8ac-174d-5792-a7fc-4ab5bbca2aae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134311 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthonormal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=\\frac{2}{3},$ $b=-\\frac{2}{3},$ $c=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|\\frac{2}{3}|+|-\\frac{2}{3}|+|-\\frac{1}{3}|=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a66add1-170c-5173-8823-07f893271a27"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a66add1-170c-5173-8823-07f893271a27" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a66add1-170c-5173-8823-07f893271a27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-632c6ed4-e8c2-5396-8c74-4461b4fdfa46" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94c4a1bf-b64c-5ddd-8ca9-6c65c5b9727e" "answer-012fe31e-f759-58b8-9e32-2deea745562c" "answer-632c6ed4-e8c2-5396-8c74-4461b4fdfa46" "answer-5a5c8c62-d50c-5ae9-8f35-24b24fc3d1ae" "answer-862d3a52-49ed-5b27-bb35-bc67945b8d32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94c4a1bf-b64c-5ddd-8ca9-6c65c5b9727e" :answer/id #uuid "94c4a1bf-b64c-5ddd-8ca9-6c65c5b9727e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-012fe31e-f759-58b8-9e32-2deea745562c" :answer/id #uuid "012fe31e-f759-58b8-9e32-2deea745562c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-632c6ed4-e8c2-5396-8c74-4461b4fdfa46" :answer/id #uuid "632c6ed4-e8c2-5396-8c74-4461b4fdfa46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a5c8c62-d50c-5ae9-8f35-24b24fc3d1ae" :answer/id #uuid "5a5c8c62-d50c-5ae9-8f35-24b24fc3d1ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-862d3a52-49ed-5b27-bb35-bc67945b8d32" :answer/id #uuid "862d3a52-49ed-5b27-bb35-bc67945b8d32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0934e8ac-174d-5792-a7fc-4ab5bbca2aae" :question/id #uuid "0934e8ac-174d-5792-a7fc-4ab5bbca2aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-41971" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]},\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{14}}{14}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis.\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{14}}{14}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{14}}{14}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthonormal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=0,$ $b=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10},$ $c=-\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|\\,0\\,|+|\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10}|+|-\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}|=\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-969beab5-314b-57a6-99da-182f476a0e29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-969beab5-314b-57a6-99da-182f476a0e29" :answer-field/id #uuid "969beab5-314b-57a6-99da-182f476a0e29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72cc1442-df79-5623-bff4-42eedddafdb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72cc1442-df79-5623-bff4-42eedddafdb9" "answer-9aa54ac6-f50b-5137-953c-f00902b1d420" "answer-77e7d035-74cb-5a21-8a35-1b0d4898e245" "answer-be937ae3-0668-5fe5-9548-61b224487acf" "answer-c38c74ea-a21b-5c0e-bb44-84641a158c8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72cc1442-df79-5623-bff4-42eedddafdb9" :answer/id #uuid "72cc1442-df79-5623-bff4-42eedddafdb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aa54ac6-f50b-5137-953c-f00902b1d420" :answer/id #uuid "9aa54ac6-f50b-5137-953c-f00902b1d420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77e7d035-74cb-5a21-8a35-1b0d4898e245" :answer/id #uuid "77e7d035-74cb-5a21-8a35-1b0d4898e245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be937ae3-0668-5fe5-9548-61b224487acf" :answer/id #uuid "be937ae3-0668-5fe5-9548-61b224487acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c38c74ea-a21b-5c0e-bb44-84641a158c8e" :answer/id #uuid "c38c74ea-a21b-5c0e-bb44-84641a158c8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133794 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ea317f2-12b0-537c-bfd8-c2c151d6c85b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ea317f2-12b0-537c-bfd8-c2c151d6c85b" :question/id #uuid "9ea317f2-12b0-537c-bfd8-c2c151d6c85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86849" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-3)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=0,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{0}{1}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-546f2176-ce65-54a2-a805-2b4a861a5018"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-546f2176-ce65-54a2-a805-2b4a861a5018" :answer-field/id #uuid "546f2176-ce65-54a2-a805-2b4a861a5018" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7edf9628-a06c-547d-b79b-2b8c3b2e00b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ea97cd7-7fc3-5a3d-bc31-abc4a8a14911" "answer-7edf9628-a06c-547d-b79b-2b8c3b2e00b4" "answer-60d1356a-94ea-5209-96d5-9d9418453443" "answer-d937650c-2bf8-5168-848d-23a4e1590bfc" "answer-a319ab1d-aad5-5d1b-8415-3377cf75bf86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea97cd7-7fc3-5a3d-bc31-abc4a8a14911" :answer/id #uuid "7ea97cd7-7fc3-5a3d-bc31-abc4a8a14911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7edf9628-a06c-547d-b79b-2b8c3b2e00b4" :answer/id #uuid "7edf9628-a06c-547d-b79b-2b8c3b2e00b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60d1356a-94ea-5209-96d5-9d9418453443" :answer/id #uuid "60d1356a-94ea-5209-96d5-9d9418453443" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d937650c-2bf8-5168-848d-23a4e1590bfc" :answer/id #uuid "d937650c-2bf8-5168-848d-23a4e1590bfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a319ab1d-aad5-5d1b-8415-3377cf75bf86" :answer/id #uuid "a319ab1d-aad5-5d1b-8415-3377cf75bf86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b568452d-b15b-5a64-b20e-4ac3b74285e9" :activity/id #uuid "b568452d-b15b-5a64-b20e-4ac3b74285e9" :activity/title "The Gram-Schmidt Process for Two Vectors" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050578 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-99574453-db24-5adc-881e-60bd9dee9204" "step-a30ac731-6001-5775-b224-b7080f289ca2" "step-84989845-fb61-500c-b47d-0a19bc3d185f" "step-74c122ae-6f5f-55d9-980e-db985